], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Working Hard", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "All in a Day's Work", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.  Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reckon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bthink or \u200bbelieve", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I reckon that you've had a hard week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are the words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pull your weight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do your part", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My team told my editor that I wasn't pulling my weight.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pick up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to learn something quickly and easily", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I suppose I've been a bit slow, but I've been trying hard to pick things up! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "training", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bprocess of \u200blearning the \u200bskills you need to do a \u200bparticular \u200bjob or \u200bactivity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The training that I received wasn't great. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pitch in ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bstart to do something as \u200bpart of a \u200bgroup, \u200bespecially something \u200bhelpful", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You've got to offer to pitch in wherever you can. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get in over one's head ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get involved in a difficult situation that is not easy to get out of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I just don't want to get in over my head.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect with Report or Comment Phrases", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about past events that have a connection to the future. </br> You can use the Present Perfect tense with other verbs to report or comment on events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use verbs such as <span class=\"italic\">reckon</span>, <span class=\"italic\">understand</span>, <span class=\"italic\">suppose</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> guess</span> and <span class=\"italic\">imagine </span>to communicate your thoughts and to report about something that happened in the past and has a connection to the present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:</br><span class=\"italic\"> I<span class=\"strong\"> understand (that) you have done</span> a lot of editing in previous jobs.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I reckon that you've had a hard week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I suppose I've been a bit slow, but I've been trying hard to pick things up! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I understand that you've been put with one of the best teams.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I imagine you've worked hard at the tasks you've been given, but you should do more than just the minimum. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Relative Clauses and Adverbial Phrases", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use relative clauses to make your writing and speaking more detailed and sophisticated. A defining clause gives essential information about a noun. A non-defining clause gives additional information about a noun.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In relative clauses, you use <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things, <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with time and <span class=\"italic\">where </span>with places.</br></br>   <span class=\"underline\">Defining Clause:</span></br></br><span class=\"italic\">  People <span class=\"strong\">who talk too much </span>annoy me a lot.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Without the clause \u201cwho talk too much\u201d, the meaning of the sentence changes:  <span class=\"italic\"></br>People annoy me a lot.</span></br></br>   <span class=\"underline\">Non-defining Clause:</span></br></br><span class=\"italic\">  My younger sister, <span class=\"strong\">who is really shy</span>, rarely speaks to anyone.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Without the clause \u201cwho is really shy\u201d the main idea of the sentence stays the same. </br> The non-defining clause is separated from the rest of the sentence with commas.  </br></br>An adverbial clause is a phrase which works like an adverb. There are several different kinds of adverbial clauses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial Clauses of Time </span></br>An adverbial clause of time indicates when something happens or how often. It begins with one of the following subordinating conjunctions: <span class=\"italic\">after</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as long as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">no sooner than</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> since</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> until</span>, <span class=\"italic\">when</span>,<span class=\"italic\"></span> or<span class=\"italic\"> while.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial Clauses of Place</span></br> An adverbial clause of place indicates where something happens. It usually starts with a preposition (e.g., <span class=\"italic\">in</span>, <span class=\"italic\">on</span>, <span class=\"italic\">near</span>) or one of the following subordinating conjunctions: <span class=\"italic\"> anywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">everywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">where</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">wherever</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial Clauses of Manner</span></br> An adverbial clause of manner indicates how something happens. It often starts with one of the following subordinating conjunctions:<span class=\"italic\"> as</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> like</span>, <span class=\"italic\"></span>or <span class=\"italic\">the way</span>. </br></br>  Look at some examples from the dialogue:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I hope that your week was better than mine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have been working hard ever since I got here. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've done everything that I've been asked to do. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The people who I work with haven't been particularly helpful either.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The training that I received wasn't great.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You've got to offer to pitch in wherever you can. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I describe a bad week at work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about problems at work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for suggestions from a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give advice and suggestions to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On a piece of paper, write down five events that made your week a very bad one at work or school. (You can invent those events, or you can use Adam's bad week).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have a conversation with a partner and tell them about your bad week at work. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask your partner for some suggestions on how to make next week better.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Switch roles. Listen to your partner talk about their bad week and give them some advice.", "type": "text"}]}]}